CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: The byte-identical key and cross-language ABI evidence supports the mechanism at the process/restart level, and the competitor comparison supports anomaly status. It does not yet fully hold at realistic ecosystem scale: prevalence is bounded to n=9 with 2 unmitigated exposures and no full-population denominator, so workload/adoption blast radius remains insufficiently evidenced for GREEN.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. This is more than integration glue because the packet combines ABI-boundary invisibility, spec-contract analysis, cross-runtime differential behavior, and generator-propagated exposure. But the shipping mechanism itself already exists in wazero, and practitioners already found adjacent fixes such as CrowdSec PR#4495 (https://github.com/crowdsecurity/crowdsec/pull/4495) and wazero issue#620 (https://github.com/wazero/wazero/issues/620). The systems insight is the synthesis, not a new runtime design. Residual A matters: successor WASI random explicitly says cryptographically secure/unpredictable and deterministic facilities only for debugging (https://github.com/WebAssembly/WASI/blob/main/proposals/random/README.md), while preview1 wording is weaker. Residual B matters more for systems altitude: bounded prevalence plus a generator amplifier is enough for a strong bug/conformance paper direction, but insufficient evidence for GREEN-scale systems generality.
